/* book exam traps: Calculator mode in tan. Convert βd = 2πd/λ to radians, keep the calculator in radian mode, and then evaluate tan βd. βd = π/4 rad is the same angle as 45°, and tan is 1. Entering 0.785 with the calculator in degree mode wrongly gives about 0.0137. | Swapping λ/2 and λ/4 behaviour. A λ/2 line repeats ZL; a λ/4 line inverts it as Z0²/ZL. | Treating an open circuit as Zin=∞ for every length. Only a zero-length open line gives infinity; a λ/4 open line gives a short at the input. | Using the lossless formula on a long lossy cable: the lossless formula repeats every λ/2 forever, but a real line drifts towards Z0; use tanh γd. | Mixing input and transfer impedance. Zin is V(0)/I(0); a transfer impedance uses a voltage at one port and a current at another. */
